{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q25100751","formula":"C₁₅H₁₃NO₂","hill":"C15H13NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":13.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diarylpropionitrile"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diarylpropionitrile (DPN), also known as 2,3-bis(p-hydroxyphenyl)propionitrile (2,3-BHPPN), is a synthetic, nonsteroidal, and highly selective agonist of ERβ (IC50 = 15 nM) that is used widely in scientific research to study the function of this receptor. It is 70-fold more selective for ERβ over ERα, and has 100-fold lower affinity for GPER (GPR30) relative to estradiol. DPN produces antidepressant- and anxiolytic-like effects in animals via activation of the endogenous oxytocin system."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":102614,"mass":239.27,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=CC=C1CC(C#N)C2=CC=C(C=C2)O)O","inchikey":"GHZHWDWADLAOIQ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2,3-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)propanenitrile","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"102614","atoms":31,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.877,"y":0.87,"z":-0.286,"el":"O"},{"x":5.936,"y":0.615,"z":0.368,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.092,"y":-2.977,"z":0.807,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.418,"y":-0.393,"z":0.377,"el":"C"},{"x":0.447,"y":0.079,"z":-0.824,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.888,"y":-0.053,"z":0.199,"el":"C"},{"x":1.898,"y":0.221,"z":-0.509,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.498,"y":0.783,"z":1.114,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.573,"y":-0.588,"z":-0.874,"el":"C"},{"x":2.395,"y":1.438,"z":-0.04,"el":"C"},{"x":2.758,"y":-0.863,"z":-0.683,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.235,"y":-1.841,"z":0.616,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.848,"y":1.095,"z":0.95,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.923,"y":-0.276,"z":-1.038,"el":"C"},{"x":3.752,"y":1.57,"z":0.255,"el":"C"},{"x":4.115,"y":-0.731,"z":-0.388,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.56,"y":0.566,"z":-0.126,"el":"C"},{"x":4.612,"y":0.485,"z":0.081,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.056,"y":0.127,"z":1.275,"el"